infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title When reset() heals vs when reset() lies
  desc Same "Try again" button — one cause clears on its own, the other is baked into the render
  compares
    - label Transient failure — reset() recovers
      children
        - label Network blip, dep mid-deploy, timed-out upstream
          desc The cause clears on its own, so a re-render genuinely succeeds
        - label Pair reset() with router.refresh()
          desc Server markup came from the server — refetch the payload, then re-render children in a transition
        - label The retry is honest
          desc The boundary unmounts and the page comes back
    - label Deterministic failure — reset() lies
      children
        - label Parsing bug, null DB field, malformed flag
          desc Nothing changed between attempts, so the render throws identically
        - label reset() re-throws instantly
          desc An auto-retrying boundary becomes a tight loop hammering the broken dependency
        - label Cap attempts, then route to support
          desc After 2 tries, link to /support instead of looping
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
